What is a Fire Fighting Vehicle?
A Fire Fighting Vehicle is a specialized vehicle equipped with a variety of fire equipment and firefighting apparatus, designed primarily for firefighting operations. It is the most basic mobile firefighting equipment. In addition, many fire departments often employ their vehicles for various other uses including emergency medical services and rescue purposes.
Fire fighting vehicles are classified into several types based on their functionality and design:
•	Conventional Fire Fighting Vehicle: Standard vehicles used for general firefighting.
•	Elevating Fire Fighting Vehicle: Equipped with extendable booms or platforms for elevated water discharge.
•	Special Fire Fighting Vehicle: Designed for specific scenarios like airport crashes or hazardous material fires.
These vehicles are essential tools for fire departments, industrial safety units, and airport rescue and firefighting (ARFF) services.
